      "generated_answer": "To test validity with an indirect truth table, assume premises true and conclusion false.  \nIf E and G are true and F is false: E\u2283F is false \u2192 violates premise; but if E=false, G=true, F=true: E\u2283F=T, G\u2283~F=F \u2192 invalid premise. Only option C gives E=T, G=T, F=F: then E\u2283F=F (invalid), so not a counterexample.  \nActually, only A works: no assignment makes premises true and conclusion false \u2014 argument is valid.  \n\n\\boxed{A}",
