ematic checking, greedy fails for exactly 20 remainders mod 25: all except when r \u2208 {0, 5, 10, 15, 20}.\n\nIn the range [1,1000], we have 1000/25 = 40 complete cycles.\n- Remainders 0,5,10,15,20 succeed: these give successful N values.\n- N = 25k + r where r \u2208 {0,5,10,15,20} are successful.\n\nFor each complete cycle: 5 successful values.\nWith 40 cycles: 40 \u00d7 5 = 200 successful values.\nBut we need N \u2265 1, so exclude N = 0.\n\nThe answer is 200.\n\n$\\boxed{200}$",
