    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{G}  \nA kinesis involves random movement changes in response to stimuli, without directionality, while a taxis involves directed movement toward or away from a specific stimulus. This distinction highlights the undirected nature of kinesis versus the oriented nature of taxis. Option G correctly captures this fundamental difference.",
      "success": true,
