    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When the valve is opened, the volume available to the vapor doubles. Since temperature is constant, the vapor pressure remains unchanged (as it depends only on temperature for a pure substance in equilibrium). The number of vapor molecules doubles because they now occupy twice the volume, but the concentration (molecules per unit volume) is halved. However, since the system was initially at equilibrium and the total amount of water is fixed, the increased volume allows more liquid to evaporate until equilibrium is reestablished, maintaining the same vapor pressure and concentration.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
