    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Using Moseley's law, K\u03b1 wavelength \u03bb \u221d 1/(Z-1)\u00b2. Given Cu (Z=29) \u03bb=1.5405 \u00c5, compute Z for \u03bb=0.7092 \u00c5 \u2192 Z\u224842 (molybdenum), and for \u03bb=1.6578 \u00c5 \u2192 Z\u224827 (cobalt). Among options, only J (Iron and Cobalt) includes cobalt, but molybdenum isn't listed; rechecking: \u03bb=0.7092 \u00c5 corresponds to Z\u224843? No\u2014calculation shows Mo (Z=42, \u03bb\u22480.7107 \u00c5), very close. \u03bb=1.6578 \u00c5 gives Z\u224827 (Co, actual Cu K\u03b1 is 1.5405, Co K\u03b1 is ~1.621 \u00c5, close to 1.6578; Fe K\u03b1 is ~1.937 \u00c5, not matching. However, option J is Iron and Cobalt, but iron's K\u03b1 is longer. Option E is Molybdenum and Nickel: Ni Z=28, \u03bb\u22481.658 \u00c5 matches second line; Mo Z=42, \u03bb\u22480.7107 \u00c5 matches first. Yes! So E: Molybdenum (Z=42) and Nickel (Z=28).\n\n\\boxed{E}",
