    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The probability that an investment does not become worthless is 80%, or 0.8. Simone loses no more than 1/3 of her investment if at least 2 out of the 3 investments survive (since losing 2 means losing 2/3, which exceeds 1/3). The probability of exactly 2 surviving is C(3,2)(0.8)^2(0.2) = 3\u00d70.64\u00d70.2 = 0.384, and the probability of all 3 surviving is (0.8)^3 = 0.512. Adding gives 0.384 + 0.512 = 0.896 \u2248 90%.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
