      "generated_answer": "We solve the recurrence $ y[n] - 3y[n-1] + 2y[n-2] = 0 $ with $ y[0] = 2 $, $ y[1] = 3 $.  \nCharacteristic equation: $ r^2 - 3r + 2 = 0 $ \u2192 roots $ r = 1, 2 $ \u2192 general solution $ y[n] = A(1)^n + B(2)^n $.  \nUsing initial conditions: $ A + B = 2 $, $ A + 2B = 3 $ \u2192 $ B = 1 $, $ A = 1 $ \u2192 $ y[n] = 1 + 2^n $.  \nThus, $ y[2] = 1 + 4 = 5 $, $ y[3] = 1 + 8 = 9 $, $ y[4] = 1 + 16 = 17 $ \u2192 sequence starts 5, 9, 17 for $ n \\geq 2 $.  \n\n\\boxed{B}",
