    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A frequency modulation (FM) receiver with input signal- to- noise ratio (S_i /nf_m) = 40 dB is used to pick- up sig-nals from different FM stations. If the transmitted FM signal is represented by km(t) = \\beta \\bullet \\omega \\bulletcos(\\omega_mt), calcu-late output signal- to- noise ratio for different values of \\beta such as 5, 10 and 105.\n\nOptions: \nA. \u03b2 = 5, 58.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 64.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 85.185 dB\nB. \u03b2 = 5, 55.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 61.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 82.185 dB\nC. \u03b2 = 5, 50 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 60 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 80 dB\nD. \u03b2 = 5, 52.5 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 58.5 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 78.685 dB\nE. \u03b2 = 5, 60.1 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 66.1 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 87.285 dB\nF. \u03b2 = 5, 47.2 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 53.2 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 73.385 dB\nG. \u03b2 = 5, 45.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 51.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 72.185 dB\nH. \u03b2 = 5, 65.7 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 71.7 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 92.185 dB\nI. \u03b2 = 5, 43.6 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 49.6 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 69.785 dB\nJ. \u03b2 = 5, 42 dB; \u03b2 = 10, 48 dB; \u03b2 = 105, 68.185 dB\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
