    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The output signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) for an FM receiver is given by:  \n$$\n\\text{SNR}_o = 3\\beta^2 \\cdot \\frac{S_i}{N_f} \\quad \\text{(in linear scale)}\n$$\nGiven $ \\frac{S_i}{N_f} = 40 \\, \\text{dB} = 10^{4} $, convert to linear scale and compute SNR for each \u03b2 using the formula.  \nAfter calculation, the closest match is option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
