    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10309",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the solution for the equationX=AX+bu;X(0) = X_0 where A=\\vert10\\vert,b=\\vert1\\vert,X_0 =\\vert- 1\\vert, \\vert- 22\\vert\\vert2\\vert\\vert0\\vert u(t) = \\delta(t) (impulse function).\n\nOptions: \nA. -3\nB. 2\nC. 0\nD. 3\nE. 10\nF. -2\nG. 22\nH. 1\nI. -10\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The equation $ X = AX + bu $ with impulse input $ u(t) = \\delta(t) $ and initial condition $ X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} $ suggests a state-space system. Solving via Laplace transform yields $ X(s) = (sI - A)^{-1}(bU(s) + X_0) $. With $ A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} $, $ b = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 2 \\end{bmatrix} $, and $ U(s)=1 $, the steady-state response to impulse is determined by the system's DC gain \u2014 but the question likely asks for the value of $ x_1(0^+) $, which jumps due to impulse. The impulse affects $ x_1 $ directly: $ \\Delta x_1 = b_1 = 1 $, so $ x_1(0^+) = -1 + 1 = 0 $.  \n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
