  {
    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10309",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the solution for the equationX=AX+bu;X(0) = X_0 where A=\\vert10\\vert,b=\\vert1\\vert,X_0 =\\vert- 1\\vert, \\vert- 22\\vert\\vert2\\vert\\vert0\\vert u(t) = \\delta(t) (impulse function).\n\nOptions: \nA. -3\nB. 2\nC. 0\nD. 3\nE. 10\nF. -2\nG. 22\nH. 1\nI. -10\nJ. -1\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The equation $ X = AX + bu $ with impulse input $ u(t) = \\delta(t) $ implies a jump condition at $ t = 0 $. Taking Laplace transforms: $ sX(s) - X_0 = AX(s) + b $, so $ (sI - A)X(s) = X_0 + b $. At $ t = 0^+ $, the state jumps by $ b $, giving $ X(0^+) = X_0 + b = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} $. Then $ X = AX $ for $ t > 0 $, so $ X(t) = e^{At}X(0^+) $. Since $ A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} $, the second component satisfies $ \\dot{x}_2 = -2x_1 + 2x_2 $, but at $ t = 0^+ $, $ x_2 = 2 $, and the question likely asks for $ x_1(0^+) = 0 $.\n\nHowever, rechecking: $ A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix} $, $ b = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} $, $ X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} $. Then $ X(0^+) = X_0 + b = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} $. The system evolves as $ X(t) = e^{At}X(0^+) $. For $ A $ diagonalizable or using Jordan form, $ e^{At} = \\begin{bmatrix}e^t & 0 \\\\ -2e^t + 2e^{2t} & e^{2t}\\end{bmatrix} $. Then $ x_1(t) = e^t \\cdot 0 = 0 $ for all $ t > 0 $, so $ x_1(0^+) = 0 $. If the question asks for $ x_1(0^+) $, answer is 0.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{C}\n$$",
      "success": true,
