    "prediction": "claude-3-haiku-20240307",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "I need to find the time-domain response using Fourier transform methods.\n\nGiven:\n- System function: H(j\u03c9) = (j2\u03c9)/(1 + 2j\u03c9)\n- Input: V(t) = cos(t)\n- Fourier transform of cos(t): \u03c0[\u03b4(\u03c9 + 1) + \u03b4(\u03c9 - 1)]\n\nThe output in frequency domain is: Y(j\u03c9) = H(j\u03c9) \u00d7 V(j\u03c9)\n\nAt \u03c9 = 1: H(j1) = (j2)/(1 + j2) = (j2(1 - j2))/((1 + j2)(1 - j2)) = (j2 + 4)/(1 + 4) = (4 + j2)/5\n\nAt \u03c9 = -1: H(-j1) = (-j2)/(1 - j2) = (-j2(1 + j2))/((1 - j2)(1 + j2)) = (-j2 + 4)/(1 + 4) = (4 - j2)/5\n\nFor the output: Y(t) contains components at \u03c9 = \u00b11\n\nY(t) = (4/5)cos(t) + (2/5)sin(t) corresponds to the magnitude and phase at these frequencies.\n\n$\\boxed{F}$",
