    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10537",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the energy stored in an inductor from t = 0 to t = 1 whose \\textphi -icharacteristic is given by \\textphi (t) = 1/3i^3 (t) and the current through it is given by i (t) = 2 sin t.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.00 J\nB. 0.75 J\nC. 1.50 J\nD. 4.00 J\nE. 2.50 J\nF. 3.00 J\nG. 1.25 J\nH. 2.75 J\nI. 2.00 J\nJ. 3.50 J\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b-instruct-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The energy stored in an inductor is given by $ W = \\int_0^1 \\frac{d\\phi}{dt} i(t) \\, dt $. Given $ \\phi(t) = \\frac{1}{3}i^3(t) $, then $ \\frac{d\\phi}{dt} = i^2(t) \\frac{di}{dt} $. Substituting $ i(t) = 2\\sin t $, we find $ \\frac{di}{dt} = 2\\cos t $, so $ \\frac{d\\phi}{dt} = (4\\sin^2 t)(2\\cos t) = 8\\sin^2 t \\cos t $. Then $ W = \\int_0^1 8\\sin^2 t \\cos t \\cdot 2\\sin t \\, dt = \\int_0^1 16\\sin^3 t \\cos t \\, dt $. Using substitution $ u = \\sin t $, $ du = \\cos t \\, dt $, limits from 0 to $ \\sin(1) $, the integral becomes $ 16 \\int_0^{\\sin(1)} u^3 \\, du = 16 \\cdot \\frac{u^4}{4} \\big|_0^{\\sin(1)} = 4\\sin^4(1) $. Evaluating numerically, $ \\sin(1) \\approx 0.8415 $, so $ \\sin^4(1) \\approx 0.502 $, and $ 4 \\times 0.502 \\approx 2.008 $, closest to 2.00 J.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 240,
        "output_tokens": 375,
        "total_tokens": 615
      },
      "provider": "local-vllm",
      "error": null
    },
    "cost": 0.00014294999999999998,
