      "generated_answer": "The equivalent resistance for resistors in parallel is given by $ \\frac{1}{R_{\\text{eq}}} = \\sum \\frac{1}{R_i} $.  \nCalculating: $ \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} + \\frac{1}{25} + \\frac{1}{30} = 0.2333... $, so $ R_{\\text{eq}} \\approx \\frac{1}{0.2333} \\approx 4.2857 $ ohms.  \nThe closest option is B (4.56 ohms), but exact calculation gives \u22484.29, and option D (4.12) is closer\u2014rechecking confirms:  \n$ \\frac{1}{10} = 0.1 $, $ \\frac{1}{15} \\approx 0.0667 $, $ \\frac{1}{20} = 0.05 $, $ \\frac{1}{25} = 0.04 $, $ \\frac{1}{30} \\approx 0.0333 $; sum = 0.29, so $ R_{\\text{eq}} = 1/0.29 \\approx 3.45 $ ohms.  \nThus, A (3.46 ohms) is correct.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
