    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The model scale is 1:20, so the head ratio is 1:20. For dynamic similarity, the head in the model should be $ h_m = \\frac{h_p}{20} = \\frac{20}{20} = 1 $ meter. Discharge scales with the cube of the linear dimensions, so $ Q_p = Q_m \\times (20)^3 = 0.5 \\times 8000 = 4000 $ m\u00b3/s \u2014 but this contradicts the options. Re-evaluating: if the head scales linearly and discharge scales with $ h^{3/2} $, then for Froude similarity, $ Q_p = Q_m \\times (L_r)^{5/2} = 0.5 \\times 20^{5/2} = 0.5 \\times 20^2 \\times \\sqrt{20} = 0.5 \\times 400 \\times 4.472 \\approx 894.4 $ m\u00b3/s.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
