      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}  \nThe study found statistically significant differences in attendance and recall rates between Sami and non-Sami populations, indicating that ethnicity may influence early outcome measures. Although the rate of screen-detected invasive cancer was not significantly different, the lower percentage of total cancers detected in the Sami group suggests disparities. These findings imply that ethnicity affects participation and screening outcomes.",
      "success": true,
