    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}  \nThe study found that changes in the lymph node microenvironment, such as reduced myeloid CD11c(+) dendritic cells and downregulated TCR zeta in CD8(+) T cells, were associated with metastases. These alterations were also present even in lymph nodes without visible metastases but located closer to the tumor. This suggests the microenvironment can serve as an early indicator of metastatic risk.",
      "success": true,
