      "generated_answer": " Norman's socialist commune failed because the workers, knowing they must work only nine hours a day, slowed their productivity, and the leadership under the Wolves was ineffective and corrupt. Additionally, Wolf stole Norman\u2019s gold-finding device, further undermining the project\u2019s viability. Ultimately, the collapse of order and morale necessitated external intervention by Norman\u2019s father and the governor to restore legitimacy and stability.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Ineffective leadership, worker demotivation due to short work hours, and theft of the gold-finding device caused the failure.}}",
