    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Benedict Arnold's death at the Battle of Quebec in 1775 led to a British victory at the Battles of Saratoga in 1777, preventing American independence. This caused the American Revolution and the French Revolution to fail, eliminating the Napoleonic Wars and altering European and global power structures. As a result, Britain retained control over its North American colonies and key historical figures like Washington and Jefferson met different fates.  \n\n\\boxed{\\text{Benedict Arnold's death led to British victory at Saratoga, preventing American independence and altering the course of global history.}}",
