    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{J}  \nDred Scott v. Sanford (1857) ruled that African Americans, free or enslaved, were not U.S. citizens and had no standing to sue in federal court, directly contradicting Garrison\u2019s argument. This decision upheld racial discrimination under the Constitution, opposing Garrison\u2019s claim of equal rights.",
