      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}\n\nThe Great Depression of the 1890s created severe economic hardship for farmers and workers, leading to widespread discontent with the existing two-party system. The platform's references to \"plundered people,\" destroyed homes, and corporate oppression directly reflect the economic crisis conditions of that decade. This economic devastation provided the primary impetus for the Populist party's rise as an alternative political force.",
